proof.text:
For every $N\ge0$, regrouping the finite sums just obtained yields
$$\sum_{n=0}^{N}|e_n|t^n\le\sum_{n=0}^{N}b_n
=\sum_{r=0}^{N}\frac1{r!}\sum_{\substack{n_1,\ldots,n_r\ge1,\ n_1+\cdots+n_r\le N}}\prod_{j=1}^{r}a_{n_j}
\le\sum_{r=0}^{N}\frac{(\sum_{j=1}^{N}a_j)^r}{r!}
\le\sum_{r=0}^{N}\frac{S^r}{r!}.$$
For the middle inequality, every tuple in the inner sum belongs to $\{1,\ldots,N\}^r$; remove the total-degree restriction, adding only nonnegative terms. Repeated distributivity identifies the unrestricted finite tuple sum with $(\sum_{j=1}^{N}a_j)^r$. The $r=0$ tuple is empty, its index sum is $0$ and its product is $1$; this also verifies $N=0$. The last inequality uses $0\le\sum_{j=1}^{N}a_j\le S$ and monotonicity of nonnegative integer powers.
